# Solubility Prediction with Molecular Descriptors

This project trains Random Forest, Extra Trees, and CatBoost regression models to predict solvent-dependent solubility (`logS`) from molecular and solvent descriptors calculated with RDKit.

## Overview

The parser creates filtered and all-entry datasets from the raw database. Each model evaluates predictions with five-fold molecule-solvent-pair-grouped cross-validation and a separate holdout test set.

The main steps are:

1. Parse and filter the BigSolDBv2.0 dataset
2. Extract solute and solvent descriptors using RDKit
3. Train Random Forest, Extra Trees, or CatBoost regressors
4. Evaluate with GroupKFold metrics, permutation importance, and holdout test metrics
5. Save model results under `results/`

