## Usage

Run the molecule-solvent-pair-grouped model:

```bash
python src/rfg_group_shuffle.py
```

This writes its metrics to `results/rfg_group_shuffle_results.txt` and will:

- load the training data from `data/processed/data_basic.csv`
- preprocess numeric and categorical features
- train the Random Forest model
- evaluate it on a molecule-solvent-pair-grouped test split

To reproduce the row-wise evaluation for comparison, run:

```bash
python src/rfg_basic.py
```

This writes metrics to `results/rfg_basic_results.txt`. The row-wise holdout may
place the same molecule-solvent pair in both partitions, so these results are
not directly comparable to pair-grouped evaluation.

A second model variant using solvent descriptors is also available:

```bash
python src/rfg_sol_desc.py
```

To train the solvent-descriptor model on all entries with valid `logS` values,
including solvents outside the whitelist used by `data_sol_desc.csv`, run:

```bash
python src/rfg_all_entries.py
```

This writes metrics to `results/rfg_all_entries_results.txt`.

Run an Extra Trees variant with the same dataset and split options:

```bash
python src/etr_group_shuffle.py
python src/etr_basic.py
python src/etr_sol_desc.py
python src/etr_all_entries.py
```

Each writes to its matching `results/etr_*_results.txt` file.

Run the CatBoost model with the same molecule-solvent-pair-grouped split and validation:

```bash
python src/catboost_group_shuffle.py
```

This writes metrics to `results/catboost_group_shuffle_results.txt`.

Run the other CatBoost variants with the same datasets and split options as the
Random Forest and Extra Trees variants:

```bash
python src/catboost_basic.py
python src/catboost_sol_desc.py
python src/catboost_all_entries.py
```

The basic variant uses a row-wise test split for comparison; solvent-descriptor
and all-entry variants hold out molecule-solvent pairs.

